ALVA — Implement the Super Jump Movement Overhaul

Objective

Implement a complete overhaul of jumping in the Alva game repository (hiyroscript/alva).

Replace the existing hold Jump to jump higher mechanic with a new universal movement mechanic called Super Jump.

The new control scheme must be:

* Normal Jump: Press Jump while grounded, without holding Down.
* Super Jump: While grounded, hold Down (the existing Fast Fall input), then press Jump.
* Air Jump: Press Jump while airborne, following the existing triple-jump rules.
* Fast Fall: Hold Down while descending in the air, as before.

Super Jump must feel like a genuinely powerful leap off the ground, not merely a normal jump with an increased height multiplier.

Normal Jump must become noticeably shorter than it currently is. Super Jump must become substantially higher than both the new Normal Jump and the game’s previous higher-jump mechanic.

Every successfully executed Super Jump must produce a visible dust burst at the fighter’s feet, originating from the ground at takeoff.

All changes must work equally for human players and CPU-controlled fighters. CPUs must understand, execute, predict, and strategically use Super Jump rather than merely being given an artificial vertical movement advantage.

Implement this as a complete, production-ready change, including gameplay physics, input handling, CPU intelligence, visual effects, documentation, localization, and automated tests.

