2. Completely replace the old higher-jump mechanic

Currently, Alva uses:

* jumpVelocity: 920
* highJumpWindow: 0.15
* highJumpHeight: 1.4

Holding Jump past a timing window activates a higher jump by modifying gravity during ascent.

Remove this behavior entirely.

Holding Jump must no longer increase jump height under any circumstances.

A Jump held for one frame and a Jump held for an entire second must produce the same Normal Jump trajectory, assuming identical starting conditions.

Do not leave behind an invisible or partial version of the old hold-to-jump-higher feature.

Retire or appropriately replace the obsolete highJumpWindow, highJumpHeight, highJumpLift, and Fighter.highJump implementation.

Remove or update references to the old mechanic throughout the CPU system, documentation, UI, and tests.

The new Super Jump must be a distinct movement action determined by the input combination at the time the jump is requested.

