14. Definition of done

This implementation is complete only when all of the following are true:

* Holding Jump no longer increases height.
* Normal Jump is noticeably shorter than before.
* Holding Down and pressing Jump on the ground immediately executes a powerful Super Jump.
* Super Jump has a visibly different, more explosive takeoff and movement arc.
* Super Jump reaches much greater height than Normal Jump.
* Every successful Super Jump leaves a brief, clear dust burst at the takeoff point.
* The dust is visible for both human and CPU fighters.
* Players can reliably perform Super Jump on the ground and on one-way platforms.
* Existing Fast Fall, platform drop, triple jump, and air-dash controls remain functional.
* Keyboard, controller, and both touch layouts support the mechanic.
* CPUs use real input combinations, understand the updated physics, and make meaningful Super Jump decisions.
* All fighters share the same new movement behavior.
* English and French UI text, controller guides, Discover, and repository documentation reflect the new mechanics.
* All relevant tests pass, including the full node --test suite.
* No unrelated gameplay features regress.

